cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, cite it as below. If you cite a measured figure, cite the commit and the split it came from."
title: "Project Scribe — Agent form-filler for grant applications using browser bypass"
version: 0.1.0
date-released: "2026-11-03"
license: CDDL-1.1
type: software
abstract: >-
  Scribe is an agent-driven form-filler for grant applications. It uses the
  same browser bypass stack as the BCC re-investigation (scrapling + curl_cffi
  headers) to navigate Cloudflare, reCAPTCHA, and JS challenges, then fills
  and submits grant applications from a structured project profile.
authors:
  - name: "Project Scribe contributors"
keywords:
  - grant applications
  - form automation
  - browser bypass
  - cloudflare bypass
  - agent tooling
  - open source
references:
  - type: software
    title: "scrapling"
    notes: "Browser automation with bypass capabilities"
    url: "https://github.com/scrapling/scrapling"
  - type: software
    title: "Project ELIZA"
    notes: "Forensic investigation suite with similar bypass stack"
    url: "https://github.com/myzticalbabe/azazael/tree/main/Project_ELIZA"